---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProfileImage from '../components/ProfileImage.astro';
import FeaturedProjectCard from '../components/FeaturedProjectCard.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const projectsSorted = (await getCollection('projects')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const featuredFallback = projectsSorted.slice(0, 3);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Jirka Schlesinger — UX Lead"
  description="UX Lead focused on complex and AI-enabled products — enterprise delivery, consulting, and practical UX leadership."
  path="/"
>
  <article class="stack-lg">
    <header class="intro-block intro-block--split intro-hero">
      <ProfileImage size="md" priority />
      <div class="intro-hero__intro">
        <h1>Jirka Schlesinger</h1>
        <p class="role-tagline">UX Lead focused on Complex & AI‑Enabled Products</p>
        <p class="role-detail">
          Designing products and leading teams for real business impact — mostly in complex enterprise and consulting environments.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="intro-hero__body">
      <p class="lede">
        I’ve spent enough time in corporate and consulting environments to know that most problems are not design problems — at least not at first.
        More often, they’re alignment problems, expectation problems, or simply the result of too many reasonable ideas colliding at once. That’s usually
        where I do my best work.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m comfortable working in ambiguity, with senior stakeholders, and in setups where budgets, governance, and delivery realities are part of the
        design space. I value calm collaboration, clear reasoning, and solutions that still make sense once the project excitement fades.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m a designer with about twenty years in design and thirteen in UX — biased toward practical outcomes, rapid prototyping when it helps us
        learn, and AI‑assisted workflows when they reduce friction instead of adding theater.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work in UX because I enjoy making complex things understandable — and complexity tends to show up wherever many people, systems, and
        priorities meet. I lead UX on digital and AI‑enabled products where requirements are “almost clear”, stakeholders are “mostly aligned”, and
        timelines are “ambitious”. My role is usually to help teams move from uncertainty to something that holds together and can be built without
        falling apart after the first release.
      </p>
      <p class="intro-closing">If you’re working on a complex product and things feel a bit fuzzy, I’m usually happy to talk.</p>
    </div>

    <section aria-labelledby="work-heading">
      <h2 id="work-heading">What I work on</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        UX, product ownership, AI‑enabled experiences, and enterprise delivery — less about polishing screens, more about avoiding unnecessary chaos.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Leading UX across discovery, design, and delivery</li>
        <li>Shaping product and platform UX in complex environments</li>
        <li>Designing experiences for AI‑driven and data‑heavy tools</li>
        <li>Turning vague ideas into concrete, defensible decisions</li>
        <li>Working closely with product owners, engineers, data teams, and senior stakeholders</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small">
        Most of this happens in enterprise or regulated contexts, where “just redesign it” is rarely an option and pragmatism tends to win over
        elegance.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="selected-heading">
      <h2 id="selected-heading">Selected work</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Described at a high level. Details are intentionally abstracted due to NDAs; the structure reflects how I work in real delivery environments.
      </p>
      <p class="muted small featured-random-note">
        Showing three projects — a random pick on each visit (JavaScript). Without JS, the first three in the catalogue appear.
      </p>

      <div class="featured-projects-row" id="featured-projects-row">
        {
          featuredFallback.map((p) => (
            <FeaturedProjectCard slug={p.slug} title={p.data.title} focus={p.data.focus} />
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div id="featured-projects-deck" class="featured-projects-deck" hidden aria-hidden="true">
        {
          projectsSorted.map((p) => (
            <FeaturedProjectCard slug={p.slug} title={p.data.title} focus={p.data.focus} />
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <script is:inline>
        (function () {
          var deck = document.getElementById('featured-projects-deck');
          var row = document.getElementById('featured-projects-row');
          if (!deck || !row) return;
          var nodes = deck.querySelectorAll('[data-featured-card]');
          var cards = Array.prototype.slice.call(nodes);
          for (var i = cards.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
            var j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
            var tmp = cards[i];
            cards[i] = cards[j];
            cards[j] = tmp;
          }
          row.innerHTML = '';
          var n = Math.min(3, cards.length);
          for (var k = 0; k < n; k++) {
            row.appendChild(cards[k].cloneNode(true));
          }
        })();
      </script>

      <p class="section-nav-links">
        <a href="/projects/">View all projects</a>
        <span class="muted"> · </span>
        <a href="/about/">Background, approach & skills</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
